#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OSGi and tools"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"This page is for readers who know **Java** but not the tools around OpenEMS: "
"OSGi, bnd, Bndtools, Gradle, Maven. It explains what OpenEMS Edge is built "
"on, which tools are involved and how they work together. Terms such as "
"OpenEMS Component, Channel and Nature are defined in "
"xref:coreconcepts.adoc[Core concepts & terminology]. Setting up the "
"environment is described in the xref:development/overview.adoc[Developer "
"Guide overview]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the Edge is built on: OSGi"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-the-edge-is-built-on-osgi
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"A normal Java program has a `+main()+` method, and all classes share the "
"classpath. The Edge is built differently: it is an **OSGi application**. "
"OSGi is a standard for modular Java programs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "The terms"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| OSGi term\n"
"| Explained for Java developers\n"
"\n"
"| **Bundle**\n"
"| A normal JAR file with additional entries in `+META-INF/MANIFEST.MF+`: name, version, which packages it makes available to others (`+Export-Package+`) and which it needs (`+Import-Package+`). Without an export, a package stays invisible to other bundles, even if it is `+public+`. Every directory `+io.openems.*+` in the repository becomes a bundle.\n"
"| **Framework**\n"
"| The program that loads, starts and stops bundles and creates a separate class loader for each bundle. OpenEMS uses **Apache Felix** (version 7.0.5). The `+main()+` method belongs to the framework, not to OpenEMS.\n"
"| **Service**\n"
"| An object that a bundle registers under an interface in a central directory (service registry). Other bundles obtain it via the interface without knowing the implementation. Example: a meter driver registers as `+ElectricityMeter+`; a Controller asks for “an `+ElectricityMeter+` with the ID meter0”.\n"
"| **Declarative Services (DS)**\n"
"| Instead of registering services by hand, you write annotations: `+@Component+` on the class, `+@Reference+` on fields to be filled with other services, `+@Activate+`/`+@Deactivate+` on start and stop methods. The DS runtime (Apache Felix SCR) creates the objects, wires them and removes them again when a dependency disappears. This is similar to dependency injection in Spring, but dynamic at runtime.\n"
"| **Configuration Admin**\n"
"| A service that stores configurations (lists of keys and values) and passes them to components. If you create a configuration, a component is created; if you change it, the component is reconfigured; if you delete it, the component disappears. The entire Edge is configured this way.\n"
"| **Metatype**\n"
"| Describes which fields a configuration has (name, type, default value, description). Input forms are generated from it automatically.\n"
"| **Event Admin**\n"
"| A simple message bus within the program. The Edge uses it to send the Cycle Events.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why OSGi?"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-why-osgi
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Device drivers, Controllers and interfaces are independent modules. A "
"manufacturer's driver only knows the API (e.g. `+ElectricityMeter+`), not "
"the other drivers."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-why-osgi
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Components can be created, changed and removed at runtime, without a "
"restart. An energy management system needs this because the hardware differs "
"from site to site."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-why-osgi
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"The same class can be instantiated any number of times (two meters of the "
"same type = two configurations)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additional bundles at runtime"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-additional-bundles-at-runtime
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"In addition to the OpenEMS bundles, the Edge contains third-party bundles. "
"The list is in `+io.openems.edge.application/EdgeApp.bndrun+`. In this "
"version of the code there are 296 bundles, 53 of them not from OpenEMS. The "
"most important:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Bundle\n"
"| Version\n"
"| Purpose\n"
"\n"
"| `+org.apache.felix.framework+`\n"
"| 7.0.5\n"
"| the OSGi framework\n"
"| `+org.apache.felix.scr+`\n"
"| 2.2.18\n"
"| Declarative Services (`+@Component+`, `+@Reference+`)\n"
"| `+org.apache.felix.configadmin+`\n"
"| 1.9.26\n"
"| Configuration Admin, stores the configuration as files\n"
"| `+org.apache.felix.metatype+`\n"
"| 1.2.4\n"
"| description of the configuration fields\n"
"| `+org.apache.felix.eventadmin+`\n"
"| 1.6.4\n"
"| events, e.g. for the Cycle\n"
"| `+org.apache.felix.fileinstall+`\n"
"| 3.7.4\n"
"| can load bundles and configurations from a directory\n"
"| `+org.apache.felix.http.jetty12+`, `+…servlet-api+`\n"
"| 2.0.8 / 6.1.0\n"
"| embedded web server (Jetty) for Apache Felix Web Console and REST\n"
"| `+org.apache.felix.webconsole+`, `+…plugins.ds+`, `+org.apache.felix.inventory+`\n"
"| 5.0.18 / 2.3.0 / 2.0.0\n"
"| Apache Felix Web Console: view and change bundles, components and configurations in the browser\n"
"| `+org.ops4j.pax.logging.pax-logging-api+`, `+…-log4j2+`\n"
"| 2.3.5\n"
"| logging (SLF4J API, output via Log4j 2)\n"
"| `+com.google.gson+`, `+com.google.guava+`\n"
"| 2.15.0 / 33.7.2\n"
"| JSON processing and helper classes; used in almost every OpenEMS bundle\n"
"| `+com.fazecast.jSerialComm+`\n"
"| 2.11.4\n"
"| serial interfaces (RS485 for Modbus RTU)\n"
"| `+bcprov+`, `+bcpkix+`, `+bcutil+`\n"
"| 1.86.0\n"
"| cryptography (Bouncy Castle)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"You do not need to download these bundles yourself; the build fetches them "
"automatically (see next section)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "The tools and how they work together"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Tool\n"
"| Needed?\n"
"| What it does\n"
"\n"
"| **JDK 25**\n"
"| yes\n"
"| Java compiler and runtime. The code is compiled for Java 25 (`+cnf/build.bnd+`, `+gradle.properties+`).\n"
"| **Git**\n"
"| yes\n"
"| Get the source code and manage changes.\n"
"| **Gradle**\n"
"| yes, included\n"
"| The build tool: compiles, tests, checks the code style and packs the JAR. It does **not** need to be installed; the repository contains the Gradle wrapper `+./gradlew+` (Windows: `+gradlew.bat+`), which downloads the matching Gradle version (9.8.1) itself on first use.\n"
"| **bnd**\n"
"| yes, included\n"
"| The OSGi tool library. It generates the OSGi manifests and component descriptions from the `+bnd.bnd+` files and annotations, resolves which bundles are needed at runtime and builds the executable JAR from them. bnd (version 7.4.0) is loaded automatically as a Gradle plugin.\n"
"| **Bndtools**\n"
"| only with Eclipse\n"
"| An Eclipse plugin that integrates bnd into the IDE: import projects, edit `+EdgeApp.bndrun+` graphically, “Resolve” and “Run OSGi” at the push of a button, templates for new bundles.\n"
"| **Maven**\n"
"| no\n"
"| Maven is **not** used as a build tool. There is, however, the file `+cnf/pom.xml+`: it lists all third-party libraries (around 115 entries) with their version. bnd reads it and downloads the libraries from **Maven Central**, the public library server. New third-party library = entry in `+cnf/pom.xml+`. The version updates in the repository (“Bump … in /cnf”) concern this file.\n"
"| **Eclipse** or **IntelliJ IDEA**\n"
"| recommended\n"
"| IDE, see xref:development/ide/eclipse.adoc[Eclipse] and xref:development/ide/intellij.adoc[IntelliJ]. According to the xref:development/coding-guidelines.adoc[Coding Guidelines], Eclipse is the officially supported development environment.\n"
"| **Node.js/npm**, **Angular CLI**\n"
"| only for the UI\n"
"| Build and start the UI, see xref:ui/setup-ide.adoc[Setup IDE].\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "From source code to the running Edge"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-from-source-code-to-the-running-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Workspace settings** are in `+cnf/+`: `+build.bnd+` (Java version, default "
"libraries `+${buildpath}+`/`+${testpath}+`, library sources), `+pom.xml+` "
"(third-party libraries), `+checkstyle.xml+` (code style rules), "
"`+formatter.properties+` (Eclipse formatter)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-from-source-code-to-the-running-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Each bundle** has a `+bnd.bnd+`. Under `+-buildpath+` it states which "
"other bundles and libraries the code may use. What is missing there is not "
"found by the compiler, even if it is in the repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-from-source-code-to-the-running-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Gradle** finds all directories with `+bnd.bnd+` via the bnd plugin and "
"treats them as subprojects. When building, it compiles the code; bnd "
"generates the manifest and puts the finished bundle under `+<bundle>/"
"generated/+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-from-source-code-to-the-running-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**`+EdgeApp.bndrun+`** in the project `+io.openems.edge.application+` "
"describes the executable program (structure see table below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-from-source-code-to-the-running-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**`+./gradlew buildEdge+`** packs all `+-runbundles+` together with the "
"framework into an executable Fat-JAR and copies it to `+build/openems-"
"edge.jar+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Entry in `+EdgeApp.bndrun+`\n"
"| Content\n"
"\n"
"| `+-runfw+`\n"
"| the framework (Apache Felix)\n"
"| `+-runproperties+`\n"
"| start parameters: web server port 8080, configuration directory `+felix.cm.dir+`, data directory `+openems.data.dir+`\n"
"| `+-runrequires+`\n"
"| the desired bundles (around 200 entries, maintained by hand)\n"
"| `+-runbundles+`\n"
"| the complete list with all dependencies and fixed versions. It is **not written by hand**, but determined by bnd (“Resolve”).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/cloud-interfaces/backend-data-transfer.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/external-interfaces/rest-control.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/external-interfaces/websocket.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"The Developer Guide describes the setup: xref:development/"
"overview.adoc[Overview], xref:development/ide/eclipse.adoc[Eclipse], "
"xref:development/ide/intellij.adoc[IntelliJ]. How to start the Edge for the "
"first time and create a first configuration is described in "
"xref:gettingstarted.adoc[Getting Started]."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Gradle explicitly requires Java 25 for compiling via a toolchain. Gradle "
"looks for an installed JDK 25; an automatic download is not set up in the "
"repository. If only a different JDK is installed, Gradle can start with it, "
"but aborts when compiling. Several JDKs side by side are not a problem."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "How the Edge is configured"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-the-edge-is-configured
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"The Edge has **no** configuration file in the sense of "
"`+application.properties+`. Everything that makes up a system (which "
"devices, which addresses, which control algorithms) is a list of **component "
"configurations** in the Configuration Admin. The ways of changing it are "
"described in xref:edge/configuration.adoc[Configuration]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structure of a configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-structure-of-a-configuration
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Each Factory has a **Factory-PID**, e.g. `+Meter.Janitza.UMG96RME+` or "
"`+Controller.Debug.Log+`. In the code it is in `+@Component(name = …)+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-structure-of-a-configuration
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"An Instance has a **Component-ID** (field `+id+`, e.g. `+meter0+`) and "
"further fields from the respective `+Config+` class (e.g. `+modbus.id+`, "
"`+modbusUnitId+`, `+type+`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-structure-of-a-configuration
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Components refer to each other via IDs: the meter names its Modbus Bridge "
"(`+modbus.id=modbus0+`), the Controller its ESS and meter."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-structure-of-a-configuration
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Some core components exist exactly once, with a fixed ID: `+_cycle+` (cycle "
"time), `+_power+` (ESS Power), `+_meta+`, `+_sum+` etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where the configuration is stored"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-where-the-configuration-is-stored
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"The Configuration Admin stores each configuration as a text file in the "
"directory `+felix.cm.dir+`. The dots of the PID become subfolders (e.g. "
"`+org/apache/felix/http.config+` for the PID `+org.apache.felix.http+`); "
"values are stored as `+key=\"value\"+`, with a type identifier for non-text "
"values. This behavior comes from Apache Felix and is not specific to OpenEMS."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-where-the-configuration-is-stored
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Default according to `+EdgeApp.bndrun+`: `+c:/openems/config+`. On macOS/"
"Linux this creates a folder named `+c:+` in the working directory (for "
"`+io.openems.edge.application+` it is in `+.gitignore+`). It is better to "
"set `+-Dfelix.cm.dir=…+` at startup."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-where-the-configuration-is-stored
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"On a device following xref:edge/deploy/systemd.adoc[Deploy on Debian/"
"Ubuntu]: `+/etc/openems.d+`, JAR in `+/usr/lib/openems+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-where-the-configuration-is-stored
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Data of the components (e.g. the local rrd4j history) is stored under "
"`+openems.data.dir+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-where-the-configuration-is-stored
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"For an empty test environment, it is enough to delete the folder before "
"starting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Creating a new bundle"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "With Bndtools templates"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-with-bndtools-templates
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS provides project templates for Bndtools (defined in "
"`+io.openems.common/bnd.bnd+`, files under `+io.openems.common/resources/"
"templates+`):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Template\n"
"| Result\n"
"\n"
"| OpenEMS Controller\n"
"| Controller with `+Config+`, `+…Impl+`, test\n"
"| OpenEMS Device\n"
"| device without a specific protocol\n"
"| OpenEMS Modbus Device\n"
"| device with Modbus connection\n"
"| OpenEMS Api\n"
"| API bundle with its own Nature\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"xref:edge/implement.adoc[Implementing a Device] shows the steps in Eclipse. "
"Without Eclipse, the easiest way is to copy a similar existing bundle and "
"rename the package, classes and Factory-PID."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adding the bundle to the Edge"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-adding-the-bundle-to-the-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid "A new bundle is built, but is **not yet** part of the Edge. To add it:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-adding-the-bundle-to-the-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Enter it in `+EdgeApp.bndrun+` under `+-runrequires+` "
"(`+bnd.identity;id='io.openems.edge.…'+`). In Bndtools: drag the bundle from "
"the __Repositories__ list to __Run Requirements__ and save."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-adding-the-bundle-to-the-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Run **Resolve** so that bnd recalculates the list `+-runbundles+`: in "
"Bndtools with the __Resolve__ button (adopt the result with __Update__), on "
"the command line with `+./"
"gradlew :io.openems.edge.application:resolve.EdgeApp+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-adding-the-bundle-to-the-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid "Commit both changes to `+EdgeApp.bndrun+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-adding-the-bundle-to-the-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"If a bundle is only entered in `+-runrequires+` and not resolved, it is "
"missing from the JAR. If Resolve reports an error, a dependency is usually "
"missing: a package that no bundle exports, or a third-party library that is "
"not in `+cnf/pom.xml+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Typical pitfalls"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Class not found when compiling**, even though it is in the repository: the "
"bundle is missing from the `+-buildpath+` of your own `+bnd.bnd+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Package not found at runtime**: the other bundle does not export the "
"package. In OpenEMS, packages are usually exported via `+package-info.java+` "
"with `+@org.osgi.annotation.versioning.Version+` and `+@Export+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Component does not start**, even though it is configured: a mandatory "
"reference (`+@Reference+` with `+MANDATORY+`) is not satisfied, e.g. wrong "
"ID in `+ess.id+`. In the Apache Felix Web Console under __OSGi → "
"Components__ you can see which reference is missing."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**New component missing in the Apache Felix Web Console**: bundle not "
"entered in `+EdgeApp.bndrun+` or not resolved again."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Gradle aborts with a toolchain error**: JDK 25 is missing (see <<sec-"
"setup,Setup>>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Eclipse after a git pull"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-eclipse-after-a-git-pull
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"A `+git pull+` changes the folders in the repository, but not the project "
"list in Eclipse. Bundles that are added or removed must be updated in "
"Eclipse by hand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Message in Eclipse\n"
"| Cause\n"
"| Remedy\n"
"\n"
"| “Project 'io.openems.edge.core' is missing required Java project: 'io.openems.common.tariff.api'”, followed by hundreds of consequential errors (“… cannot be resolved to a type”, also for `+org.osgi+` and `+org.junit+`)\n"
"| A bundle from the `+-buildpath+` is in the repository, but not imported into Eclipse.\n"
"| __File → Import → General → Existing Projects into Workspace__, select the repository as root, tick all projects that are not grayed out, do **not** tick “Copy projects into workspace”.\n"
"| “The project does not have a bnd.bnd file” and almost everywhere “The container 'Bnd Bundle Path' references non existing library '…/generated/….jar'”\n"
"| Eclipse still has a project whose `+bnd.bnd+` no longer exists (e.g. a removed bundle whose `+bin+` and `+generated+` folders were left behind). In one observed case, Bndtools built no JARs while it was in the workspace, not even for `+io.openems.wrapper+` and `+io.openems.common+`.\n"
"| Delete the project in Eclipse (right-click → __Delete__, do **not** tick “Delete project contents on disk”). In that case, the workspace built again afterwards.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"To check: every folder with `+bnd.bnd+` in the repository must exist as a "
"project in Eclipse, plus `+cnf+`. Conversely, every Eclipse project except "
"`+cnf+` needs a `+bnd.bnd+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid "Further notes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Do not build with Gradle and Eclipse at the same time.** Both write to the "
"same `+generated/+` folders. If you call `+./gradlew+` in between, select "
"all projects in Eclipse afterwards and refresh them with F5."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Wait after “Clean all”.** Clean deletes all generated JARs. While around "
"250 projects are rebuilt, the Problems view temporarily shows many errors. "
"Only evaluate them after the build has finished (__Window → Show View → "
"Progress__)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Reading the error list:** The entries of type “Build Path Problem” and "
"“Bndtools …” are important. The many “cannot be resolved” errors are almost "
"always consequential errors."
msgstr ""

